WEBVTT

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:11.090
Can you imagine...

00:00:11.090 --> 00:00:16.300
...a life in which you could never
touch the one you love?

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:18.560
He takes the life of whatever he touches.

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:21.980
That was the curse the witch put on him.

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:23.850
His own mother has
distanced herself from him.

00:00:23.850 --> 00:00:26.190
His friends have called him a monster.

00:00:26.190 --> 00:00:31.360
Even strangers have spoken of him as the
Death incarnate that dwells in the forest.

00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:33.030
And yet,

00:00:33.030 --> 00:00:36.280
he doesn't feel the least bit lonely.

00:01:05.190 --> 00:01:07.350
Caught you, you naughty girl!

00:01:07.350 --> 00:01:08.650
Mother!

00:01:08.650 --> 00:01:11.900
You've got to stay in bed in
your room like a good little girl.

00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:15.360
Alice, you have a weak
constitution, you know.

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:17.780
I'm sorry.

00:01:17.780 --> 00:01:19.990
I'm not mad at you.

00:01:19.990 --> 00:01:22.410
I'm just worried about you, Alice.

00:01:25.290 --> 00:01:26.870
Good morning, everyone!

00:01:26.870 --> 00:01:28.330
Good morning!

00:01:29.580 --> 00:01:31.800
Good morning, Sharon and Alice.

00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:33.130
Good morning.

00:01:33.130 --> 00:01:37.590
Sharon, could you show me how to
do something on the sewing machine?

00:01:37.590 --> 00:01:41.220
All right. I'll be there right
after I take Alice to her room.

00:01:41.220 --> 00:01:43.560
I found some bugs in the kitchen...

00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:46.180
Sprinkle salt water on the floor.

00:01:46.180 --> 00:01:49.100
Keep at it for several days
and see how it goes.

00:01:49.100 --> 00:01:52.230
That's our head maid!
You can count on her.

00:01:52.230 --> 00:01:54.400
Yeah, isn't she something?

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:57.570
Although I must say she lacks
the character of a head maid.

00:01:57.570 --> 00:01:59.820
Ooh, how rude of you to say that!

00:01:59.820 --> 00:02:03.160
You want character?
I'll give you character!

00:02:03.160 --> 00:02:05.120
You ready? Here's your character!

00:02:06.330 --> 00:02:07.410
What the heck was that?

00:02:07.410 --> 00:02:09.830
Oh, dear, was it that strange?

00:02:09.830 --> 00:02:11.580
What did you think of it, Alice?

00:02:11.580 --> 00:02:12.880
It was perfect.

00:02:12.880 --> 00:02:16.010
Oh, my! You're too easy on me!

00:02:17.800 --> 00:02:21.300
Your Grace? Please don't run
in the house, okay?

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:23.300
Okay! I'm going outside now!

00:02:31.940 --> 00:02:37.360
Why, Alice! Have you made
friends with His Grace?

00:02:37.360 --> 00:02:43.120
Were you hoping to see him? Is that why
you were walking around the house?

00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:45.950
Oh, my.
That's a long, hard road you tread.

00:02:45.950 --> 00:02:49.370
But I won't stand in your way.

00:02:49.370 --> 00:02:50.920
Forgive me for teasing you.

00:02:50.920 --> 00:02:54.540
It's just that your face is so
cute when you blush, Alice.

00:02:54.540 --> 00:02:56.920
Good morning, Sharon.

00:02:58.090 --> 00:02:59.880
Good morning, Rob.

00:02:59.880 --> 00:03:02.430
And good morning to you too, Alice.

00:03:03.930 --> 00:03:06.260
You always hide behind
your mother's skirt, don't you?

00:03:06.260 --> 00:03:08.140
You've got such a scary face, that's why.

00:03:08.140 --> 00:03:09.640
There's nothing to be
scared of, little girl.

00:03:09.640 --> 00:03:12.480
It doesn't help when you
say that with a straight face...

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:14.020
Have you gotten used
to life in the mansion?

00:03:14.020 --> 00:03:14.810
Uh-huh.

00:03:14.810 --> 00:03:17.610
What do you think of the way
that your mother works?

00:03:17.610 --> 00:03:19.530
She's really amazing!

00:03:19.530 --> 00:03:24.780
When I grow up, I want to be
a fine maid just like her... sir.

00:03:24.780 --> 00:03:27.540
My daughter's so adorable I could cry...

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:29.910
But you already are.

00:03:29.910 --> 00:03:35.000
I look forward to the day when
we can work together, Alice.

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:36.170
Good day.

00:03:43.050 --> 00:03:47.180
Okay, I'm going to work now,
so stay in bed like a good little girl.

00:03:47.180 --> 00:03:48.180
Okay.

00:03:50.390 --> 00:03:52.770
My sweet Alice,

00:03:52.770 --> 00:03:55.810
I'll protect you no matter what.

00:03:55.810 --> 00:03:57.440
I love you!

00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:43.880
"Episode 10: The Duke, Alice,
and a Song for Two"

00:05:48.300 --> 00:05:51.850
Ooh, Mother's majorly pissed.

00:05:51.850 --> 00:05:56.730
The fact that Walter and I were both gone
on Christmas might've been the last straw.

00:05:56.730 --> 00:06:01.770
It's all your fault, Walter,
for following me without my knowledge.

00:06:01.770 --> 00:06:06.240
It's all his fault,
my brother the firstborn.

00:06:16.250 --> 00:06:17.460
Oh, wait, that's right.

00:06:18.460 --> 00:06:21.540
I wonder if she's going to be okay...

00:06:21.540 --> 00:06:25.340
Look, I know we just met, so I shouldn't
be saying this, but let's face it.

00:06:25.340 --> 00:06:28.800
Cuff is such a useless good-for-nothing,
and you know why? It's all because of...

00:06:28.800 --> 00:06:30.720
...you, her childhood friend!

00:06:30.720 --> 00:06:31.300
Huh?

00:06:31.300 --> 00:06:34.220
You look out for her too much,
and that's a habit you've got to break.

00:06:34.220 --> 00:06:38.100
You should let her do the shopping by
herself sometimes. It's for her own good.

00:06:38.100 --> 00:06:40.400
F-For Cuff's own good?

00:06:40.400 --> 00:06:41.480
Hmm?

00:06:42.810 --> 00:06:45.530
Viola may have a point there.

00:06:45.530 --> 00:06:49.490
But still, I'm worried, so I'm watching
Cuff from a distance just in case.

00:06:49.490 --> 00:06:52.070
I'm not going to bail her
out today, I promise!

00:06:52.070 --> 00:06:54.450
Huh?! H-Hey, wait!

00:06:54.450 --> 00:06:56.330
All right, will that be all, dear?

00:06:57.870 --> 00:06:59.910
Yep, that's everything
that was on the note.

00:06:59.910 --> 00:07:01.370
Thanks! Bye now!

00:07:01.370 --> 00:07:03.250
Now hold on, miss.
Where's the cash you owe me?

00:07:03.250 --> 00:07:05.920
--Cash?
--That's right. Cash.

00:07:05.920 --> 00:07:11.010
Hmm, Zain's not with me today,
so I don't know what to do...

00:07:11.010 --> 00:07:13.350
Argh, what the heck is she doing?

00:07:13.350 --> 00:07:15.850
I want to bail her out.
Bail her out right now.

00:07:15.850 --> 00:07:18.560
No, this is exactly the
habit I've got to break.

00:07:18.560 --> 00:07:20.600
I've got it! Is it all right
if I trade you for it?

00:07:20.600 --> 00:07:22.480
--What?!
--Of course it's not all right!

00:07:22.480 --> 00:07:23.690
You're putting the lady on the spot here!

00:07:23.690 --> 00:07:26.570
Check out this cat-shaped rock I found!

00:07:26.570 --> 00:07:29.150
I was planning on giving it to Zain,
but what the hay?

00:07:29.150 --> 00:07:30.700
Nobody's going to want that!

00:07:30.700 --> 00:07:31.740
Oh, this is so awkward...

00:07:31.740 --> 00:07:34.620
Didn't your folks give you
some money to pay for this?

00:07:34.620 --> 00:07:37.200
Oh, so "cash" means "money"?

00:07:37.200 --> 00:07:38.620
Sorry about that.

00:07:38.620 --> 00:07:40.580
All right, thanks!

00:07:40.580 --> 00:07:41.790
Come again!

00:07:44.000 --> 00:07:45.920
Here you go! Fresh from the oven.

00:07:45.920 --> 00:07:49.090
Thanks. This is money.
Some people call it cash.

00:07:49.090 --> 00:07:51.050
Yeah well, I knew that.

00:07:51.050 --> 00:07:53.180
She paid the bill without a hitch.

00:07:53.180 --> 00:07:55.600
You're making progress, Cuff!

00:08:01.890 --> 00:08:04.310
Such nice, soft bread.

00:08:04.310 --> 00:08:05.520
I'll protect you for as long as I live.

00:08:05.520 --> 00:08:07.110
For as long as you live?
That's kind of unlikely.

00:08:14.280 --> 00:08:15.280
Sorry.

00:08:16.160 --> 00:08:17.580
Wait a sec.

00:08:17.580 --> 00:08:21.540
Zain trusted me with that money.

00:08:21.540 --> 00:08:23.120
I'd get in trouble if you took it.

00:08:23.120 --> 00:08:24.580
L-Let go of me!

00:08:26.040 --> 00:08:27.040
Watch out!

00:08:32.220 --> 00:08:33.550
Are you all right?

00:08:33.550 --> 00:08:34.880
Y-Yeah.

00:08:34.880 --> 00:08:38.100
I tried to pickpocket you, and yet you...
I'm sorry.

00:08:38.100 --> 00:08:39.430
Well, now you know better.

00:08:39.430 --> 00:08:40.270
Aw, shoot!

00:08:40.270 --> 00:08:42.850
The stuff Zain asked me to buy...

00:08:42.850 --> 00:08:46.230
Hey there. Let's pick this all up
now and head on home.

00:08:46.230 --> 00:08:49.020
I see that habit of yours
has reared its ugly head again.

00:08:49.020 --> 00:08:51.190
I don't think I'll ever
be able to kick it.

00:09:05.830 --> 00:09:06.830
Your Grace?

00:09:07.830 --> 00:09:09.710
Are you having trouble sleeping again?

00:09:09.710 --> 00:09:11.550
Yeah, sort of.

00:09:11.550 --> 00:09:16.630
I thought I might get a little drowsy
if I took a walk around the mansion.

00:09:16.630 --> 00:09:18.760
Shall I get in bed with you?

00:09:18.760 --> 00:09:21.770
Get in bed with me?!
And must you get so close to say it?!

00:09:21.770 --> 00:09:24.390
I'll go to my room and get some pajamas.

00:09:24.390 --> 00:09:26.640
Please wait for me in
your bedroom, Your Grace.

00:09:26.640 --> 00:09:29.190
Hey, hang on there...

00:09:29.190 --> 00:09:31.650
The whole thing's been settled
with none of my input.

00:09:35.400 --> 00:09:36.650
May I come in?

00:09:39.740 --> 00:09:41.660
Y-You really mean to go through with this?

00:09:41.660 --> 00:09:42.910
Why, of course.

00:09:44.250 --> 00:09:47.670
I'll try to stay as still as I can.

00:09:47.670 --> 00:09:51.040
You can leave as soon as I fall asleep.

00:09:51.040 --> 00:09:53.170
As you wish.

00:09:53.170 --> 00:09:56.590
The one I love is lying beside me...

00:09:56.590 --> 00:10:00.180
It's kind of... freaking me out...

00:10:00.180 --> 00:10:03.180
Totally... freaking me out...

00:10:05.230 --> 00:10:09.440
She's got long eyelashes...
and beautiful lips.

00:10:10.690 --> 00:10:13.270
You're my angel.

00:10:14.610 --> 00:10:17.780
Do you think staring at me
will help you fall asleep?

00:10:17.780 --> 00:10:19.660
So, you noticed, huh?

00:10:19.660 --> 00:10:22.030
Maybe she's a devil, not an angel.

00:10:26.660 --> 00:10:31.040
I'm feeling kind of tense now, and it's
made it even harder for me to fall asleep.

00:10:31.040 --> 00:10:33.250
I know what you mean.

00:10:33.250 --> 00:10:35.010
Can I take off my pajamas?

00:10:35.010 --> 00:10:36.460
No! Why?

00:10:36.460 --> 00:10:41.090
I always sleep in the nude when I'm in my
room, so this feels kind of uncomfortable.

00:10:41.090 --> 00:10:43.220
Well, now's definitely not a good time!

00:10:43.220 --> 00:10:44.890
I'll try to make the best of it.

00:10:44.890 --> 00:10:47.100
I wouldn't say she's a devil...

00:10:47.100 --> 00:10:48.560
...she's more of a succubus.

00:10:48.560 --> 00:10:50.730
Your Grace?

00:10:50.730 --> 00:10:53.690
I pictured you as a succubus just now!

00:10:53.690 --> 00:10:55.070
Did I look good?

00:10:55.070 --> 00:10:56.740
Yeah, you did!

00:10:56.740 --> 00:11:00.450
Come on, isn't it about time
you really tried going to sleep?

00:11:00.450 --> 00:11:02.490
You're starting to strip again!

00:11:02.490 --> 00:11:04.780
I just don't feel comfortable
in these pajamas.

00:11:04.780 --> 00:11:08.160
What if Rob saw us now?
How would we explain it?

00:11:08.160 --> 00:11:10.960
It looks like I'm doing
something nasty to you!

00:11:12.040 --> 00:11:13.710
Do you want to try something nasty?

00:11:13.710 --> 00:11:15.630
You're the one who's
being nasty right now!

00:11:17.960 --> 00:11:24.800
Now that I think about it, it's not right
for an unwed couple to sleep together.

00:11:24.800 --> 00:11:29.600
My mother's really straitlaced,
so I doubt she'd approve of it.

00:11:29.600 --> 00:11:35.440
Your Grace? How do you feel about your
mother... I mean, the lady of the house?

00:11:39.440 --> 00:11:42.320
I don't have any strong feelings
for her one way or the other now.

00:11:42.320 --> 00:11:46.990
Like Walter said, she has been
waiting for me this whole time.

00:11:46.990 --> 00:11:51.370
And I do want to have a seat
at the family dinner table again.

00:11:51.370 --> 00:11:54.130
If I can break this curse,
I think I can make peace with her.

00:11:54.130 --> 00:11:57.420
And when I do, I'll tell her about us.

00:11:57.420 --> 00:12:01.800
I know it's not easy for an heir
to marry his maid.

00:12:01.800 --> 00:12:03.840
But I'll make a serious effort to ask her.

00:12:03.840 --> 00:12:07.430
If my family doesn't approve,
I'll break ties with them and--

00:12:07.430 --> 00:12:09.430
You mustn't.

00:12:09.430 --> 00:12:12.390
You mustn't even consider it.

00:12:12.390 --> 00:12:14.440
Please, just don't.

00:12:14.440 --> 00:12:15.440
Please?

00:12:17.900 --> 00:12:20.570
Well, I'll cross that bridge
when I get to it.

00:12:20.570 --> 00:12:22.150
First, I've got to break this curse.

00:12:22.150 --> 00:12:24.160
That'll get the ball rolling.

00:12:25.950 --> 00:12:27.870
I think I can get to sleep now.

00:12:27.870 --> 00:12:30.450
Thanks. You can go now.

00:12:30.450 --> 00:12:32.250
As you wish.

00:12:35.500 --> 00:12:37.090
Good night, Alice.

00:12:37.090 --> 00:12:39.130
I hope I can see you again in my dreams.

00:12:40.420 --> 00:12:42.510
Then I shall see you in your dreams.

00:12:42.510 --> 00:12:44.470
Good night, Your Grace.

00:13:00.360 --> 00:13:01.900
It's still warm.

00:13:16.460 --> 00:13:17.710
He's right.

00:13:17.710 --> 00:13:19.420
Once his curse is broken,

00:13:19.420 --> 00:13:23.550
His Grace will go back to his family's
main residence as its heir.

00:13:23.550 --> 00:13:27.220
And he'll live with his family once again.

00:13:27.220 --> 00:13:29.100
That's the way it should be.

00:13:29.100 --> 00:13:30.100
And yet...

00:13:36.230 --> 00:13:37.940
Why, Alice, it's you!

00:13:37.940 --> 00:13:40.230
I'm sorry to bother you so late at night.

00:13:49.160 --> 00:13:50.410
Rob!

00:13:51.790 --> 00:13:53.950
Oh, you don't have to
put out your cigarette.

00:13:53.950 --> 00:13:55.790
I'm sorry to bother you
during your break time.

00:13:55.790 --> 00:13:57.870
I wanted to show you these!

00:13:57.870 --> 00:13:59.540
Alice gave them to me.

00:13:59.540 --> 00:14:04.300
She told me she knitted them for a little
bit each day as she thought of me!

00:14:04.300 --> 00:14:10.300
With the scarf and mittens Alice made me,
I'll stay warm no matter how cold it gets.

00:14:10.300 --> 00:14:11.300
Oh...

00:14:12.640 --> 00:14:14.560
Come on, say something.

00:14:14.560 --> 00:14:19.350
You really have begun
to smile more, Your Grace.

00:14:19.350 --> 00:14:22.440
It's a far cry from your nihilistic days.

00:14:22.440 --> 00:14:24.530
Don't remind me!

00:14:24.530 --> 00:14:27.360
Even I look back on those days and wince.

00:14:27.360 --> 00:14:29.110
Your Grace?

00:14:29.110 --> 00:14:30.910
I made you some tea.

00:14:30.910 --> 00:14:32.330
Okay, I'm on my way!

00:14:35.040 --> 00:14:38.160
Oh, and try not to smoke too much, okay?

00:14:38.160 --> 00:14:39.670
Yes, Your Grace.

00:14:41.000 --> 00:14:42.710
Back then...

00:14:42.710 --> 00:14:47.470
...after His Grace had been cursed
and I was ordered to care for him,

00:14:47.470 --> 00:14:49.340
I honestly didn't know what to do.

00:14:50.590 --> 00:14:53.260
It wasn't that I was afraid of his curse.

00:14:53.260 --> 00:14:57.770
It was just that I'd never
raised a child before.

00:14:57.770 --> 00:15:04.230
I feared that I wouldn't be able to bring
him up alone without a woman's help.

00:15:04.230 --> 00:15:06.820
Still, he was the family's precious son.

00:15:08.240 --> 00:15:10.450
Your right eye is really scary-looking.

00:15:13.070 --> 00:15:14.780
Will this do?

00:15:14.780 --> 00:15:16.040
Uh-huh.

00:15:16.040 --> 00:15:20.290
I considered it an honor to be
entrusted with such an important task.

00:15:20.290 --> 00:15:25.880
However, as he grew older,
His Grace and I began to butt heads.

00:15:25.880 --> 00:15:31.800
He fought with me and ran away
I don't know how many times.

00:15:31.800 --> 00:15:38.020
Eventually, His Grace shut himself in his
room and began to retreat into his shell.

00:15:38.980 --> 00:15:42.480
I suspect that his loneliness
had turned into fear.

00:15:44.940 --> 00:15:49.320
More and more often he
expressed a desire to die.

00:15:49.320 --> 00:15:53.820
"If only His Grace had someone
his own age to talk with," I thought.

00:15:53.820 --> 00:15:57.540
And the first person that
came to my mind was...

00:15:57.540 --> 00:15:59.120
...her.

00:16:00.410 --> 00:16:02.420
Me, a maid?

00:16:02.420 --> 00:16:06.170
Does this mean I could
see His Grace again?

00:16:06.170 --> 00:16:10.880
It was obvious that Alice had
been mistreated by her aunt.

00:16:10.880 --> 00:16:17.350
Even so, she bowed deeply to
the woman before we departed.

00:16:17.350 --> 00:16:25.270
Now, Alice is even more dear to His Grace
than I could have possibly imagined.

00:16:28.780 --> 00:16:33.490
But Alice knows where
she stands in all of this.

00:16:33.490 --> 00:16:35.740
She knows it only too well.

00:16:36.490 --> 00:16:39.120
I'm weird, aren't I?

00:16:39.120 --> 00:16:40.950
How so?

00:16:40.950 --> 00:16:47.130
I hope that His Grace will break his curse
and live with his family once again.

00:16:47.130 --> 00:16:52.840
And yet, His Grace is
fond of me, his maid.

00:16:52.840 --> 00:16:55.220
While I appreciate his affection,

00:16:55.220 --> 00:16:59.680
when I think about how that
might estrange him from his family,

00:16:59.680 --> 00:17:03.140
I can't take any pleasure in it.

00:17:03.140 --> 00:17:06.150
You're not weird at all.

00:17:06.150 --> 00:17:09.480
It's up to the two of you to
decide how you'd like to be,

00:17:09.480 --> 00:17:12.070
so I'll keep my opinions to myself.

00:17:12.070 --> 00:17:16.280
But the feelings you have for
His Grace aren't weird at all.

00:17:16.280 --> 00:17:18.780
They're something purer.

00:17:18.780 --> 00:17:21.490
I might go so far as to call it...

00:17:21.490 --> 00:17:22.790
...fate.

00:17:25.250 --> 00:17:26.540
That's what it is.

00:17:32.840 --> 00:17:33.880
Rob?

00:17:35.220 --> 00:17:37.840
You're going to get cold pretty soon.

00:17:37.840 --> 00:17:40.390
Come join us for a cup of tea.

00:17:40.390 --> 00:17:42.560
All right, I'll be there shortly.

00:17:45.140 --> 00:17:48.360
If the two of them are happy,

00:17:48.360 --> 00:17:50.900
then so am I.

00:18:23.430 --> 00:18:25.430
So... How was it?

00:18:25.560 --> 00:18:29.810
It was superb. A wonderful
and moving experience.

00:18:29.810 --> 00:18:31.650
Th-Thanks.

00:18:31.650 --> 00:18:35.030
You played a cheerful song this time.

00:18:35.030 --> 00:18:38.410
Although I thought the ballad you played
last time was wonderful, too.

00:18:38.410 --> 00:18:39.610
R-Really?

00:18:39.610 --> 00:18:41.870
Well, I'm glad you liked it.

00:18:41.870 --> 00:18:45.250
This isn't my way of thanking you
for the mittens, though.

00:18:45.250 --> 00:18:46.830
I don't know how to put it, but...

00:18:46.830 --> 00:18:52.500
...I'm just really glad to be able
to spend time with you like this.

00:18:52.500 --> 00:18:53.920
Me, too.

00:18:53.920 --> 00:18:58.050
Now that we're alone, Your Grace,
my body aches with yearning.

00:18:58.050 --> 00:19:00.260
So, what should I play next?

00:19:00.260 --> 00:19:01.390
Say, Alice?

00:19:01.390 --> 00:19:04.310
Why don't you sing to my
accompaniment once in a while?

00:19:04.310 --> 00:19:05.930
Who, me?

00:19:05.930 --> 00:19:11.940
Yeah, you've sung for me several
times now. I like what you sing, Alice.

00:19:11.940 --> 00:19:14.980
Very well. What would you like me to sing?

00:19:14.980 --> 00:19:16.820
All right, how about...

00:19:35.590 --> 00:19:37.760
"The Owl and the Pussy-cat"?

00:19:37.760 --> 00:19:39.510
Yeah. Sing it for me.

00:19:48.020 --> 00:19:58.610
♬ The Owl and the Pussy-cat went to sea
In a beautiful pea green boat, ♬

00:19:58.610 --> 00:20:07.740
♬ They took some honey, and plenty of money,
Wrapped up in a five pound note. ♬

00:20:07.740 --> 00:20:16.590
♬ The Owl looked up to the stars above,
And sang to a small guitar, ♬

00:20:16.590 --> 00:20:18.170
Take it from here, Mr. Owl.

00:20:18.170 --> 00:20:19.460
You want me to sing?

00:20:22.430 --> 00:20:26.810
♬ 'O lovely Pussy! O Pussy my love, ♬

00:20:26.810 --> 00:20:30.140
♬ What a beautiful Pussy you are,
You are, You are! ♬

00:20:30.140 --> 00:20:35.060
♬ What a beautiful Pussy you are!' ♬

00:20:35.060 --> 00:20:41.700
♬ Pussy said to the Owl,
'You elegant fowl! ♬

00:20:41.700 --> 00:20:47.830
♬ How charmingly sweet you sing! ♬

00:20:47.830 --> 00:20:57.090
♬ O let us be married!
too long we have tarried: ♬

00:20:57.090 --> 00:21:05.930
♬ But what shall we do for a ring?' ♬

00:21:18.360 --> 00:21:19.610
Your Grace...

00:21:19.610 --> 00:21:21.440
Your face is as red as a beet.

00:21:21.440 --> 00:21:22.780
Don't look at me!

00:21:22.780 --> 00:21:26.200
I can't believe my heart would start
pounding over some nursery rhyme lyrics.

00:21:26.200 --> 00:21:28.740
I felt kind of embarrassed, too.

00:21:28.740 --> 00:21:30.870
I didn't know you could feel that way.

00:21:30.870 --> 00:21:34.710
What kind of person do you think I am?

00:21:34.710 --> 00:21:36.170
I may have been embarrassed,

00:21:36.170 --> 00:21:38.670
but it doesn't bother me
because of you, Your Grace.

00:21:38.670 --> 00:21:40.420
I-I think I'd better call it a night...

00:21:40.420 --> 00:21:42.630
...while I can still think straight.

00:21:44.340 --> 00:21:47.300
Lately I've been feeling kind of cheerful.

00:21:47.300 --> 00:21:49.680
I wonder if that's why I could
write a song like that.

00:21:49.680 --> 00:21:51.640
That could be the reason.

00:21:51.640 --> 00:21:55.140
You have definitely been smiling
more often, Your Grace.

00:21:55.140 --> 00:21:56.850
I owe it all to you, Alice.

00:21:56.850 --> 00:22:00.860
As long as I don't lose hope, I think that
one day I'll be able to break my curse.

00:22:03.820 --> 00:22:06.320
Once I do that, I'll be able to
return to my family's home.

00:22:06.320 --> 00:22:07.610
Proudly...

00:22:07.610 --> 00:22:09.700
And I'll take you with me.

00:22:09.700 --> 00:22:12.370
Well, this is where I'll say good night.

00:22:12.370 --> 00:22:14.950
You don't have to walk me to my room.

00:22:14.950 --> 00:22:16.960
O-Oh, really? What a bummer...

00:22:17.830 --> 00:22:20.090
Good night, Your Grace.

00:22:20.090 --> 00:22:21.710
You blew me a kiss!

00:22:22.880 --> 00:22:25.760
Forgive me, Your Grace.

00:22:25.760 --> 00:22:28.680
I'm just a lowly servant.

00:22:30.510 --> 00:22:32.970
Your Grace, no matter what you may think,

00:22:32.970 --> 00:22:34.350
when that fateful day arrives,

00:22:34.350 --> 00:22:37.480
we won't be able to see
each other freely anymore.

00:22:37.480 --> 00:22:42.270
I know this, and it saddens me.

00:22:45.110 --> 00:22:47.860
I'm a no-good maid.

00:22:47.860 --> 00:22:49.990
Aren't I, Mother?

00:22:49.990 --> 00:22:52.120
Alice!

00:22:52.120 --> 00:22:53.200
Your Grace...

00:22:53.200 --> 00:22:55.580
Let me walk you to your room.

00:22:55.580 --> 00:22:59.330
It may not be very far, but you never
know what may be lurking outside.

00:22:59.330 --> 00:23:01.670
I appreciate the sentiment,

00:23:01.670 --> 00:23:04.460
but a servant can't let her
master walk her to her room...

00:23:04.460 --> 00:23:06.720
It doesn't matter.

00:23:06.720 --> 00:23:10.140
I'd like to treat you like a lady, Alice.

00:23:11.890 --> 00:23:12.930
What's wrong?

00:23:13.930 --> 00:23:15.850
Even if it hadn't panned out...

00:23:17.060 --> 00:23:22.480
...I believe the pussy-cat would still
have been happy to have loved the owl.

00:23:22.480 --> 00:23:27.110
Is that what that nursery
rhyme was all about?

00:23:28.650 --> 00:23:30.240
Hey! Wait up, Alice!

00:23:30.240 --> 00:23:32.660
I'll be your escort!

00:23:32.660 --> 00:23:35.200
Hey! Did you hear me, Alice?

00:23:42.750 --> 00:23:45.960
"The Duke of Death and His Maid"

00:23:42.750 --> 00:23:45.960
"The Duke and Secret Magic."
